TEXT -1888 -1176 Left 5 ;This example shows a large 14bus system with 220kV and 110kV circuits\nwith 10x 110kV cables(1x1000mm2 oil) with length of 3km till 5km \nand 7x 400kV overhead lines 4x240mm2 with 20 to 40km length \none PV-element in Bus3 (V=400kV,P=-300MW)\none PV element in Bus9  (V=116kV,P=-80MW till -150MW) and a slack in bus1 (V=400kV)\nThe 10 constpower loads are 100MW/20MVAr\nThe loads , pv-slacks, vslack, c-batt and transformes are all with controlling nodes\nso you can change many parameters of the circuit during simulation \nlike transformeer phase angle or voltage translation factor, voltage level of slack, \nshape of a loadvalue as function of time and also switching off loads, transformers \nat a specific timepoint. \nIn this example only pv-element at bus9 and c-batt elements are varied\nYou can change other parameters as exercise\nTry also switching off lines or cables from startup by changing the on-parameter to zero
